# Negative test: log an uncorrected (UC) error that also carries yellow
# TES bits. bff_mce_notify() checks `mce->status & MCI_STATUS_UC` and bails
# out (TES is undefined for uncorrected errors per the driver comment)
# before ever checking TES, so this must produce no reset/overflow report.
#
# The POLL keyword forces mce-inject's non-exception/logged-only path
# (MCJ_EXCEPTION cleared) instead of the default behavior of raising a real
# synchronous #MC exception for UC errors, so this injection is safe to run
# and still reaches the MCE decoder notifier chain via machine_check_poll().
CPU 0 BANK 3
MCGSTATUS TES_P
STATUS UNCORRECTED TES_YELLOW
POLL
